#+TITLE: cadgui — a Qt6 GUI CAD host on embedded ECL (release-3.0 epic)
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: epic
#+DEPENDS: -
#+TARGET: release 3.0
#+BRANCH: qt6-gui
#+DATE: 2026-11-09
#+UPDATED: 2026-11-16 (restructured from qt6-drawing-canvas-first-increment into this epic + per-phase sub-issues)

* Goal

Grow clautolisp into a near-AutoCAD/BricsCAD-parity CAD, built as close to 100%
by AI agents as possible: Common Lisp backend, Qt6 UI, on Windows/macOS/Linux,
every interaction scriptable/testable, the GUI detachable/offscreen for
headless screenshots. The GUI is a fourth clautolisp HOST -- *cadgui* -- the
graphical peer of cadtui on the cador core. ("cadgui" is the working name; a
marketing name comes later.)

This is the master/index issue. The work is decomposed into per-phase
sub-issues (below); detail lives there, decisions and status live here.

* Settled architecture decisions (the load-bearing ones)

- *Embed ECL, in-process* (not a subprocess): the production architecture is
  clautolisp ported to ECL and embedded in the Qt app. (Supersedes the earlier
  subprocess + sexp-wire "protocol v2" sketch.) [[cadgui-1-ecl-port]]
- *Our own thin Qt6 Widgets C++ shell* embedding ECL (not lqml / not a
  CFFI-direct binding): reuses the existing Qt6 Widgets code
  (=clautolisp/tools/clautolisp-gui-qt/=), keeps control, and its C boundary is
  the seed of the CRX ABI. Validated by two spikes
  (=clautolisp/tools/clautolisp-gui-qt/spike-ecl-embed/=): ECL computes a
  display list, Qt6 paints it, offscreen -> PNG; and a nested-QEventLoop
  interactive input loop that survived a 2000-point / ~8M-cons GC-stress run.
  [[cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host]]
- *cadgui = the fourth host* (nihil / cador / cadtui / cadgui), a UI-tree host
  over the cador core, reusing the cadtui ui-tree classes, rendered graphically
  by the embedded-ECL Qt6 canvas. =clautolisp --host cadgui= established in the
  CLI in 2.4.21 (renderer WIP). [[cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host]]
- *One Action Layer, four surfaces* (GUI, -command CLI, script/AutoLISP, AI
  driver) with a CI driveability guard -- cross-cutting, established WITH the
  GUI, makes "testable" and "AI-driveable" the SAME work. [[cadgui-action-layer]]
- *3D is a separable, demand-gated module* (OpenCASCADE + ACIS), not on the
  2D critical path. [[cadgui-5-3d-file]] [[cadgui-6-3d-gui]]
- *CRX = an ARX/BRX-LIKE own C ABI* -> SOURCE compatibility (recompile against
  CRX headers), not binary drop-in of real ARX/BRX. [[cadgui-4-crx-api]]

* Phase order + sub-issues (committed, pjb 2026-11-09)

| # | sub-issue                     | what                                    | status  | depends |
|---+-------------------------------+-----------------------------------------+---------+---------|
| 1 | [[cadgui-1-ecl-port]]         | port clautolisp to ECL (embed target)   | DONE    | -       |
| 2 | [[cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host]]     | the cadgui host: Qt6 canvas on embed ECL| NEXT    | 1       |
| 3 | [[cadgui-3-2d-parity]]        | full 2D user compatibility              | planned | 2       |
| 4 | [[cadgui-4-crx-api]]          | CRX: the C/C++ extension ABI            | planned | 2       |
| 5 | [[cadgui-5-3d-file]]          | 3D file support (OCCT + ACIS)           | planned | 3       |
| 6 | [[cadgui-6-3d-gui]]           | 3D GUI (BricsCAD-like)                   | planned | 5       |
| X | [[cadgui-action-layer]]       | Action Layer (cross-cutting)            | planned | 2       |

Sequencing: 2D-complete + CRX (phases 1-4) is a shippable, extensible 2D CAD;
3D (5-6) is demand-gated. The Action Layer is built WITH phase 2 so every later
phase registers through it and driveability never regresses.

* Effort — scoping, NOT a schedule

Earlier revisions carried several calendar estimates (person-years, then
"recalibrated agent-throughput", then a "maximal-agent" month table). *Treat
them all as relative scoping, not dates.* Measured reality: phase 1 (the ECL
port) was estimated at ~2-6 weeks and landed, green, in a single working
session -- a 50-100x miss. Observed agent throughput makes calendar figures
non-predictive, so this epic tracks by PHASE COMPLETION and per-slice
acceptance, not by time. Relative difficulty order still holds: phase 5
(ACIS/OCCT round-trip) is the long pole; phases 2 and 4 are expertise-bound
(event-loop embedding, ABI design); 1 and the 2D breadth of 3 are throughput-
bound.

* How we build it: implement -> test -> document, every slice

Each phase decomposes into *buildable slices*, and a slice is not done until all
three are:
- *Implement*: the slice lands behind a flag / host where it does not regress
  the others; CL code in the owning subsystem, C++ in the Qt6 shell.
- *Test*: CL logic -> fiveam in the subsystem's =/tests= (the project's standard,
  already green on SBCL/CCL/ECL); the canvas -> OFFSCREEN render tests (golden
  image / display-list assertions, the spike's =-platform offscreen= path);
  interaction -> SCRIPTED nested-event-loop tests (spike #2's pattern) run
  headless in CI. Wherever an interaction is an Action-Layer action, its headless
  API test is the one the driveability guard REQUIRES.
- *Document*: each host/module gets a spec + user-manual .org built INCREMENTALLY
  with the slices (as cador has =clautolisp-cador-spec.org= and cadtui its
  specification), plus =--list-hosts= / =-h= surfaces and the Action-Layer
  =describe-action= docstrings. A slice updates its doc in the same change.

The Action Layer ([[cadgui-action-layer]]) is the substrate that makes
test-and-drive one thing: the layer a headless test drives is the layer the GUI
and an AI driver drive, and a CI guard fails the build when an interaction is
not registered, typed, documented and headless-tested.

* Status board

- Phase 1 (ECL port): *DONE* -- suite green on ECL 24.5.10, merged to master
  (MR !555), clautolisp/alfe 2.4.20. [[cadgui-1-ecl-port]]
- Phase 2 (cadgui host): *ACTIVE* -- Qt-API decided, two spikes validated, the
  =--host cadgui= CLI identity established (2.4.21). Next: the cadgui module +
  canvas. [[cadgui-2-qt6-gui-host]]
- Phases 3-6 + Action Layer: planned, scoped in their sub-issues.

